---
// Deck Section 06 — Relational lens
---

<section class="bg-cream py-24 md:py-[120px]">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1180px] px-6">
    <p class="text-xs font-medium tracking-widest uppercase text-coral mb-8">The product philosophy</p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-5xl md:text-6xl text-navy leading-tight tracking-tight max-w-2xl mb-6">
      We look at products with a relational lens.
    </h2>
    <p class="text-base text-navy-muted max-w-lg mb-16 leading-relaxed">
      Software is the most direct relationship businesses have with their customers.
    </p>

    <!-- Two-column comparison -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-px rounded overflow-hidden" style="background: #d8d0a8;">
      <div class="p-8 md:p-12 bg-cream-deep">
        <p class="text-xs font-medium tracking-widest uppercase text-navy-muted mb-8">The default lens</p>
        <ul class="flex flex-col gap-5">
          {[
            "Optimise for in-app metrics.",
            "DAU, session length, retention curves.",
            "Features shipped per quarter.",
            "The app is the product.",
          ].map((line) => (
            <li class="text-base text-navy-muted leading-relaxed border-b border-cream pb-5 last:border-0 last:pb-0">{line}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="p-8 md:p-12 bg-navy">
        <p class="text-xs font-medium tracking-widest uppercase text-coral mb-8">The relational lens</p>
        <ul class="flex flex-col gap-5">
          {[
            "Optimise for the user’s real life.",
            "Did they meditate this morning? Did they actually go for the run?",
            "Did they get more done?",
            "The app is the means. The change in their life is the product.",
          ].map((line) => (
            <li class="text-base text-cream leading-relaxed border-b pb-5 last:border-0 last:pb-0" style="border-color: #3d3870;">{line}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Chain -->
    <div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 text-base text-navy-muted">
      {["Real-life impact", "customer success", "retention", "LTV"].map((step, i) => (
        <>
          <span class="font-serif text-xl text-navy">{step}</span>
          {i < 3 && <span class="text-coral text-xl" aria-hidden="true">→</span>}
        </>
      ))}
      <span class="text-sm italic ml-2">That order matters.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
